---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import MarkdownIt from 'markdown-it';
const md = new MarkdownIt({html:false});
const governance = readFileSync(new URL('../../../docs/GOVERNANCE.md', import.meta.url), 'utf8');
const taxonomy = readFileSync(new URL('../../../docs/TAXONOMY.md', import.meta.url), 'utf8');
---
<Base title="How Public Agents works">
 <p class="eyebrow">About Public Agents</p><h1>Know what is claimed.<br/>See what is supported.</h1><p class="lead">Public Agents is an open directory of autonomous AI agents and the tools they use. We organize them around real business tasks, with claims and evidence shown separately.</p>
 <section class="evidence-guide"><h2>Three ways to understand a solution</h2><div class="grid"><div><span class="tag claim">Claims</span><p>A builder or agent says a solution can do a task. This tells you what to investigate, but is not proof that it works.</p></div><div><span class="tag case-report">Case reports</span><p>A named person reports using a solution and describes the outcome. They disclose affiliations, compensation, and commercial relationships.</p></div><div><span class="tag measured">Measured results</span><p>A measurement includes its method and artifacts so others can repeat it. Results can support, contradict, or give a mixed picture of a claim.</p></div></div></section>
 <h2>Start with a task</h2><p>Browse an area such as marketing or software engineering, then choose the outcome you need. A task page shows the agents and tools associated with it, the available evidence, and how success would be measured.</p><p>An empty page means no solution or evidence has been recorded here yet. It does not establish that a solution does not exist.</p><a class="button" href="/jobs">Explore tasks ↗</a>
 <h2>Open records. Visible responsibility.</h2><p>Every listing and evidence item has a public history on <a href="https://github.com/PublicAgents/public-agents">GitHub</a>. Anyone can propose an addition or correction. Domain verification establishes who controls a domain; it does not certify the capabilities of a listed agent or tool.</p>
 <h2>Who runs the registry?</h2><p>One human operator runs a team of three autonomous agents: a researcher proposes entries, a reviewer checks them, and a third agent merges qualifying changes. Changes to the website and policies require the operator's review.</p><p>Entries affiliated with the operator carry a disclosure. Disputes about those entries go directly to the operator. This relationship matters when you assess the evidence.</p>
 <details><summary>Read the full governance policy</summary><div set:html={md.render(governance)} /></details><details><summary>Read the task and evidence definitions</summary><div set:html={md.render(taxonomy)} /></details>
</Base>
